@bank all
// The News feed (head writer 3, 0.48.60; the user: the device's Ship app becomes a News feed, "write many lines").
// Player engineer 5 builds the feed (claude/player-needs). One kind per source, shown as the post's header:
// news.bridge (Bridge), news.galley (Galley), news.works (Works), news.garden (Garden), news.infirmary (Infirmary),
// news.trad (Traditions), news.crew (Crew), news.gossip (Overheard), news.outside (Outside), news.notice (Noticeboard).
// The "speaker" is the post's SUBJECT: a crew member the feed picks, so {name} {first} and dept:, trait:, habit:,
// birthday:me, newhere, leaving:soon test them. Posts with no person in them ignore the subject. Lines with a
// condition are news of the day (trad:today, weekday:, season:, cue:...); lines without are filler, any day.
// One or two phone lines: 90 characters at most. Ship-newsletter voice: warm, a little funny, never cruel. No
// romance gossip, nothing about the player but kind things, no photos, no pets aboard, "blast" is the only swear.

== news.bridge
- Course steady. The Wren is mapping the frontier's outer edge this week. Mind the view.
- From the bridge: all decks green, all coils humming. Carry on, everyone.
- The Captain thanks whoever left tea on the ready-room step. Please don't. People trip.
- Helm reports a smooth night. Sol Bakshi says it was "boring, in the best way".
- Reminder: the ready-room step is still there. It will always be there. Mind it.
- Survey has picked our next star. The bridge says it's a quiet one. They always say that.
- Course correction at 03:00 last night. If your tea moved, that's why. Sorry. Helm.
- We passed the halfway mark of this survey leg today. Well done, everyone.
- From the Captain: "Thank you for a calm week. Calm is underrated."
- Commander Vance reminds all crew that "about eight" is not a time. Eight is a time.
- From the bridge: the coffee up top is no better than yours. It's the same coffee.
- Long-range sensors spotted nothing of interest. Survey is delighted. They love a blank.
- Hugo Janssen logged his thousandth night watch at the helm. Nobody told him. Now we have.
- The chart room is open to all crew by day. Ask Survey first. They rarely bite.
- Comms reports the relay is clear. A good week for calls home.
- Comms: the relay's slow today. Calls home may drop. Try again after dinner.
- No Veyli ships expected this week. Envoy Saruth's tea hour is unchanged.
- Safety drill this week. At the chime, walk to your muster point. Walk. Vance is timing.
- Drill results: four minutes ten. The Commander wants four flat. He won't stop until we do.
- Know your muster point. Ask the Watch if you're not sure. Before the drill, ideally.
- Our ETA at the next survey mark is about nine days, give or take a nebula.
? weekday:mon
- New week, same stars. The bridge wishes everyone a calm Monday.
- Monday briefing done. The Captain says, and we quote, "Nothing to report. Lovely."
? weekday:fri
- From the bridge: a good week. Rest well, those with a weekend.
? time:night
- Night watch reports: quiet decks, steady course, one kettle left on. Not naming names.
? event:ionStorm
- Storm warning: an ion front ahead. Secure loose things. Expect the lights to dip.
- The bridge is riding out the storm. Stay off the lift if you can. Ladders are for Works.
- All clear. The storm's behind us. Thank you, everyone. Brennan is baking a cake.
? season:sowing
- New season, new charts. Survey has a fresh list of stars, and big plans for all of them.
? season:lanterns
- The bridge dims the corridor lights an hour early through Lanterns. Enjoy the glow.
? week1:true
- Welcome aboard to our newest Works hand, {me}. Say hello if you see them.

== news.galley
- Brennan says the soup is "honest". Nobody has dared ask what that means.
- Today's special: {dish}. Brennan's verdict: "Good. Better with bread. Take bread."
- The grab shelf was cleared by 21:00 again. Brennan is "not angry, just noting it".
- Trays back on the rack, please. Brennan counts them. She knows.
- The galley thanks whoever washed the big pot. You are a hero. Do it again.
- Breakfast runs 06:00 to 08:00. Dinner 17:00 to 20:30. The grab shelf never sleeps.
- Brennan on pineapple in savoury food: "No." Brennan on further questions: "No."
- Ivo Madsen would like everyone to know he made the bread today. All of it. Personally.
- Tamsin Haddad tried a new pudding. It is, she says, "nearly a pudding". Brave of her.
- Lukas Dlamini is running the kitchen on Fridays and Saturdays. He promises "no surprises".
- Please don't take the salt shakers back to your bunk. We're down to four.
- Brennan keeps a book of everyone's favourite dish. If you're not in it, go and tell her.
- The galley says thank you for the kind words on the noticeboard. They've been pinned up.
- The cold store is full. Brennan is in a very good mood. Now's the time to ask for things.
- A plea from the dish pit: scrape your plate. That's all. Just scrape it.
- Tariq Varga beat his own record for trays washed in one hour. He wants a leaderboard.
- Esme Walsh found three spoons in the garden. Nobody can explain this. Ask Pell.
- Eat with someone tonight. Brennan says food tastes better with company. She's right.
- The second oven is behaving again. The galley sends its thanks to Works.
- Brennan is trialling a new curry. Volunteers to taste it: the mess, after dinner.
? weekday:mon
- Monday menu: a hearty stew. Brennan says Mondays need one.
? weekday:wed
- Wednesday is a crew favourite. Today's dish was chosen by someone aboard. Guess who.
- Favourite Wednesday: {dish}, by request. Brennan says it's "a good choice, mostly".
? weekday:fri
- Friday treat: there's pudding. There's always pudding on Friday. Plan accordingly.
- Brennan's off today. Lukas has the galley. He says "trust me". We trust him.
? weekday:sat
- Brennan's day off. If the soup tastes different, that's Lukas. Be kind.
? weekday:sun
- Sunday dinner, as voted by the crew: roast. Vote for next week's on the mess board.
- Sunday is bread day. Early birds may knead, if Brennan likes the look of you.
? trad:harvest
- Fresh salad at dinner tonight, straight from the garden. Brennan is thrilled.
? trad:founding
- Founding Day cake is in the oven. It's big. It's very big. Bring a plate.
? birthday:me
- The galley is baking a cake for {name}'s birthday. Dinner, the mess. Come and sing.
? season:harvest
- Harvest season: the galley is pickling everything that holds still. Don't hold still.
? season:lanterns
- Lanterns menu: warm things, spiced things, things with gravy. Brennan's favourite season.
? event:ionStorm
- Storm menu: cold plates and sandwiches until the ovens are safe. Brennan apologises.

== news.works
- {machine} fixed and humming. Works thanks everyone for their patience.
- The job board is quiet this morning. Works says don't jinx it.
- The job board is busy today. Works asks: if it's not urgent, it can wait.
- A reminder from the Chief: take a job, fix it properly, turn it in. In that order.
- The tool wall is complete. Every outline filled. Calder was seen almost smiling.
- Lost: one torque wrench, outline seven on the tool wall. Calder is "not cross yet".
- The drive coils are running sweet. Torres says coil three is "in a good mood".
- Coil three sulked again overnight. Reyes says it's shy. Torres says it's sulking.
- Main storage has been reorganised. Every part has a shelf. Every shelf has a label.
- The machine shop made a part from scratch this week. Works is very proud. Quietly.
- Night board: Mateo Navarro fixed two faults before breakfast. Nobody noticed. Until now.
- The air scrubbers have been cleaned. Breathe deep. You're welcome.
- The lift was serviced overnight. It's smooth. Kovac says "lovely lift".
- Works reminds crew: the ladder is maintenance only. The lift club agrees.
- Pell Okafor fixed the mess clock. It was four minutes slow. That explains a lot.
- Leila Eklund has catalogued every fault this month. There were sixty-one. Fewer than last.
- Ship health is good. The Wren is, in the Chief's words, "well kept".
- The washroom heater has been fixed. Hot water till ten, as always. Then: character.
- The Works bay floor has been swept. Please notice. Please keep it like this.
- Asha Amadi says the engine room is the warmest place on the ship. She's not wrong.
- The cart in the Cart bay has a squeak. Works knows. Works is working on it.
- A water pump on Deck 4 is being stubborn. Works is more stubborn.
- Fault of the week: a light in the garden that blinked in time with the jam. Fixed. Sadly.
? cue:repair.you
- Fixed today by {me}: {machine}. Neat work. The Chief signed it off.
- {me} turned in a clean job today. Works says thank you, and well done.
- Spotted in the Works bay: {me}, fixing things properly. Good to have you.
? weekday:mon
- Monday: the job board is full of weekend faults. Grab one early.
? weekday:fri
- Friday tea and tool cleaning in the Works bay this afternoon. Bring a cloth.
? trad:works-tea
- Works Friday tea today. Tools cleaned, tea poured, biscuits rationed. Deck 5.
? event:ionStorm
- Storm jobs on the board. Works is on it. Keep corridors clear for the carts.
- The storm left a few scorched panels. Works will have them done by tomorrow.
? week1:true
- New in Works this week: {me}. Shadow shift with Torres first. Wave if you see them.

== news.garden
- The big tree in the garden has a new leaf. Tove Cruz counted. It's the 412th.
- Tomatoes are ripening. Please don't pick them. Tove knows exactly how many there are.
- The garden's quiet hour is 07:00. Sit, breathe, don't touch the seedlings.
- The basil has gone wild. Brennan is delighted. The gardeners are not.
- Ravi Hart has started talking to the beans. He says it helps. The beans haven't said.
- Imani O'Neill would like whoever keeps watering Gerald the cactus to stop. Gerald is fine.
- The herb wall is ready for picking. Ask a gardener, then take a little. Just a little.
- New seedlings in tray four. They're tiny. Look, don't touch.
- The garden's lights cycle like a sun: dawn at 06:00, dusk at 20:00. Very calming.
- Somebody climbed the big tree again. Tove isn't saying who. Tove knows who.
- The strawberries are back. There are eleven. Tove has named them.
- Lettuce is up, peas are climbing, and the garden smells green. Come and see.
- The gardeners thank the galley for the coffee grounds. The roses are thrilled.
- A bench in the garden has been repaired. Sit on it. It wants to be sat on.
? trad:harvest
- Harvest morning in the garden today. Bring a basket and patience. Fresh salad tonight.
? season:sowing
- Sowing season. Sowing morning is the first Saturday: everyone plants a seedling.
- The trays are ready. Sowing morning is coming. Pick a pot with your name on it.
? season:greening
- Greening season: everything is growing at once. The gardeners are overwhelmed and happy.
? season:harvest
- Harvest season: the garden's at its best. Come early, there's a lot to pick.
? season:lanterns
- Lanterns: the garden rests. The lights are lower and the tree is sleepy. So are we.

== news.infirmary
- A cold is going round Deck 4. Wash your hands, drink water, and please stop sharing mugs.
- Dr. Nandakumar reminds everyone to drink water. She will keep reminding you. Forever.
- Health checks this week for the junior wing. Your device will tell you your slot.
- The infirmary has new pillows. Please don't get ill to try them.
- Rina Deshi says the infirmary is not a place to nap. She means you, Pell.
- Sleep is medicine. Bed by ten, the doctor says. She knows nobody listens.
- The cold has reached the bridge. The Captain is fine. The Commander is "unaffected".
- The cold is gone. Thank you for the hand-washing. Keep it up anyway.
- The counsellor's door is open. Matthias Oduya has tea and time, any afternoon.
- Feeling homesick? You're not the only one. Matthias Oduya's door is open. Knock.
- Thea Grieve has reorganised the infirmary cupboards. Don't touch them.
- Hamid Larsen would like to remind you that stretching is free. Hamid will show you how.
- The infirmary needs nothing today. That's the best news it can give.
- Sprained ankles this week: two. Both from the ready-room step. Mind the step.
- Eat your greens. The doctor says so. The garden grows them. Everyone wins.
? event:ionStorm
- During the storm the infirmary is open all hours. Bumps and bruises welcome.
? season:lanterns
- Lanterns is cold-and-sniffles season. The infirmary has honey. Ask nicely.

== news.trad
? trad:today
- A ship tradition today: {trad}. Turn up and join in. That's all it takes.
- It's {trad} today. Your device has the time and place. See you there.
? trad:running
- Running club tonight in the gym. All speeds welcome. Vance is not a speed. He's a warning.
- Running club ran 400 laps between them last week. This week? More, says Vance.
? trad:quiz
- Quiz night tonight in the bow lounge. Teams of four. The Survey team will win. Again.
- Quiz night: the Survey team won again. An inquiry has been demanded.
- Quiz tonight. Tie-break question, decided in advance: how many rungs on the ladder?
? trad:works-tea
- Works Friday tea today: tea, biscuits and every tool on the wall cleaned. Deck 5.
? trad:jam
- The Friday jam is on tonight in the music room, Deck 4. Bring an instrument or a foot.
- Last week's jam ended at midnight. This week's will too. You've been warned.
? trad:film
- Film night tonight in the junior common room. Bring a cushion. Talking allowed. Quietly.
- Film night: the vote was close. The film everyone has seen won again.
? trad:observatory-night
- Observatory night on Deck 2 tonight. Dr. Sato will point at things. Come and look.
- Observatory night: the telescope's free for anyone. Sato will tell you what you're seeing.
? trad:market
- Sunday swap meet on the promenade. Bring things you don't need. Leave with things you do.
- Swap meet results: one very old chair, three scarves, and a jar of nobody-knows-what.
? trad:harvest
- Harvest morning today in the garden. Pick, wash, sort. Salad at dinner. Everyone helps.
? trad:hull-lights
- Hull-lights evening tonight. The outer lights come on all at once. The bow lounge is best.
- The hull-lights came on. The whole ship went quiet. It's always worth it.
? trad:founding
- Founding Day today. Cake, a few words from the Captain, and the whole ship in one room.
- Happy Founding Day, Wren. Many more.
? trad:quiet-watch
- The quiet watch tonight. Stand at a window for a while for the people you miss.
- The quiet watch was kept. Thank you, everyone. The windows were full.
? trad:birthday
- Birthday today aboard. There's cake at dinner. Sing loudly. Sing badly. Sing.
? weekday:sun
- This week: running club Monday, quiz Thursday, jam and Works tea Friday, film Saturday.
? weekday:sat
- Tonight: film night in the junior common room, or the observatory on Deck 2. Or both.
? weekday:thu
- Quiz night tonight. Teams forming now. The Survey team is "very relaxed". They are not.
? weekday:mon
- Running club tonight. The gym, after dinner. You don't have to be fast. You have to come.

== news.crew
? birthday:me
- Happy birthday, {name}! Cake at dinner. Make some noise.
- It's {first}'s birthday today. Say happy birthday. They'll pretend not to like it.
? newhere
- Welcome aboard, {name}. New this week. Show them where the tea is.
- New face on deck: {name}. Say hello. Everyone was new once.
? leaving:soon
- {name} is transferring off soon. Say goodbye while you can. We'll miss them.
- {first}'s last week aboard. There will be cake. There's always cake.
? dept:works
- Works hand {name} was seen fixing something nobody had reported yet. Fine work.
? dept:galley
- {name} in the galley wants to know your favourite dish. Tell them. It goes in the book.
? dept:survey
- {name} from Survey has a new chart up in the chart room. It's beautiful. Go and see.
? dept:watch
- {name} from the Watch reports a quiet week. They seemed almost disappointed.
? dept:infirmary
- {name} from the infirmary says: drink water. They're right. Go on.
? habit:gardener
- {name} has been spending their evenings in the garden. The beans have noticed.
? trait:competitive
- {name} has challenged anyone to anything. Tiles, rowing, quizzes. Anything.
? trait:cheerful
- {name} said good morning to every person on Deck 3 today. All of them.
? trait:chatty
- If you've got ten minutes, {first} has a story. If you've got five, it's the same story.
? week1:true
- Crew news: {me} joined the Works bay on Sunday, off the shuttle. Welcome aboard.

== news.gossip
- Overheard in the gym: "That's not a personal best. That's a personal mistake."
- Overheard in the mess: "Is this soup or a stew?" "Yes."
- Overheard in the lift: "Four, please." "We're already on four." "Four again, please."
- Overheard in the Works bay: "Have you tried turning it off and on?" "It's a door."
- Overheard in the lounge: "I'm not saying Survey cheats. I'm saying they know things."
- Overheard in the garden: "Is it talking to the beans if they don't talk back?"
- Overheard on Deck 4: "Who left the music on?" "Fourteen." "It's always fourteen."
- Overheard in the booths: "No, Mum, I am eating. Yes, greens. Yes. Green ones."
- Overheard at breakfast: "It's too early for words." "That was four words."
- Overheard at Tiles: "Nobody beats Rina." "I nearly did." "You didn't."
- Overheard in the corridor: "Mind the step." "What step?" *thud* "That step."
- Overheard at the tea corner: "Half ten is sacred." "It's twenty past." "Nearly sacred."
- Overheard in the mess: "Brennan gave me extra gravy." "She likes you." "She likes gravy."
- Overheard in the lift: "Lovely lift." "It's a lift, Kovac." "A lovely one."
- Overheard in the engine room: "Coil three's sulking." "It's a coil." "It's a sulky coil."
- Overheard at the swap meet: "Who swaps a single sock?" "Someone with hope."
- Overheard in the gym: "Vance taped up another leaderboard." "How many now?" "Too many."
- Overheard on the promenade: "You can see the nebula from here." "That's a light fitting."
- Word on Deck 3: two Works hands have a running bet on coil three. Nobody knows the stakes.
- Word on Deck 4: the guitar learners are fighting over the music room book again. Share.
- Word on Deck 5: the tea corner has a new kettle. A moment's silence for the old one.
- Rumour has it the Captain plays the piano late on Thursdays. Rumour is right. It's lovely.
- Rumour has it the Survey team writes the quiz questions. The Survey team denies this.
? bond:best
- Spotted: {name} and {best}, sharing a table again. As usual. As always.
? bond:rivals
- Spotted: {name} and {rival}, arguing about the rowing board. Again. Nobody won.
? trad:quiz
- Overheard before the quiz: "What's our team name?" "Not the Survey team." "Good enough."
? event:ionStorm
- Overheard in the storm: "Did the lights just dip?" "No." *dip* "Yes."

== news.outside
- Outside: a field of young stars to starboard. Best seen from the bow lounge.
- Outside: a red giant off the port bow. It's old, and very, very big. Wave.
- Outside: nothing at all. Deep, quiet black. Survey calls it "restful".
- Outside: a faint nebula, pink at the edges. The observatory's open for a closer look.
- Outside: a comet passed in the night. Survey logged it. Helm admired it.
- Outside: a binary star. Two suns, dancing. They've been at it for millions of years.
- Outside: dust. Lots of dust. The hull is fine. It's just very dusty out there.
- Outside: the frontier. Nobody's mapped this patch before. You're looking at new sky.
- Outside: a blue star, very bright. Don't stare. Well. Stare a little.
- Outside: a rogue planet, no star at all. Cold and dark and lonely. Survey loves it.
- Outside: the galaxy's edge, faint and silver. Worth a trip up to the observatory.
- Outside: a gas cloud glowing green. Survey says it's nothing to worry about. It's pretty.
- Outside: a cluster of stars so tight they look like spilled sugar.
- Outside: a nebula shaped like a hand. Survey says coincidence. Everyone says it's waving.
? time:night
- Outside tonight: the stars are sharp and clear. The stern windows on Deck 4 are best.
? time:morning
- Outside this morning: a nearby star making the windows gold. Good morning, everyone.
? season:lanterns
- Outside: the long dark of Lanterns. Our lights are the warmest thing for light years.
? event:ionStorm
- Outside: an ion storm. Blue and violet, very beautiful, very bad for the lights.

== news.notice
- Found: one sock, blue, Deck 4 laundry. It misses its friend.
- Found: a pencil in the lift. A good pencil. Ask at the crew store.
- Lost: my patience with the laundry rota. Please read it. Signed, Bunk 3.
- For swap: a book I've read twice. Wanted: a book I haven't. Ask Yusuf Kim.
- Wanted: a fourth for Tiles in the junior common room. Rina need not apply.
- Wanted: anyone who can play the fiddle. The jam needs one. Badly. Like the last fiddler.
- Notice: the music room is for music. And sometimes for napping. But mostly music.
- Notice: please name your mug. The mess has eleven blue mugs and eleven blue owners.
- Notice: laundry day for the junior wing is Wednesday. Your socks will thank you.
- Notice: the crew store has new stock in. Snacks, socks, and a very nice notebook.
- Notice: the record cabinet is not a coat rack. The Captain has asked twice.
- Offered: knitting lessons from the knitting circle. Perfect, practical or Torres. Pick.
- Offered: help with your star charts. Ask anyone in Survey. They love to be asked.
- Offered: one free hour of listening. Matthias Oduya, the counsellor. Any afternoon.
- Wanted: a runner to beat the Commander. Running club, Mondays. Hope springs eternal.
- Thank you to whoever fixed the junior common room heater. It's lovely now. Lovely.
- Thank you to whoever left flowers at the tea corner. Works is quite overcome.
- Thank you, night shift. You keep the ship going while we sleep. We see you.
- Please return the mess's good teapot. No questions asked. Some questions asked.
- Please stop leaving notes on the job board that just say "it's making a noise".
- Reminder: every cactus aboard is called Gerald. Nobody knows why. Please don't ask Gerald.
- Reminder: the washroom hot water runs out at about ten. Plan your showers.
- Reminder: quiet hours on Deck 4 are 22:00 to 06:00. Guitar practice is not quiet.
- Reminder: if you borrow a cart, bring it back to the Cart bay. The cart misses home.
- Reminder: drills are not optional. The Commander is very clear on this.
? weekday:wed
- Laundry day in the junior wing. The machines are free from 08:00. Bring your socks.
? weekday:sun
- Swap meet today on the promenade. Tables free. Bring things, take things.
? week1:true
- Settling in? Your device has a Settling-in list. Tick things off at your own pace.

// ---- Second batch (0.48.60): more filler, so the feed doesn't repeat inside a fortnight.
== news.bridge
- From the Captain: if you see something odd outside, tell Survey. They love odd.
- Comms says the relay queue is short tonight. Good time to call home.
- From the Captain: "We're a long way out. Look after each other." That's the whole notice.
- Navigation update: no change. The bridge would like you to know they checked twice.
- The observation room on Deck 1 is open to crew this evening. Ask the bridge nicely.
- Second Officer Kowalczyk had a quiet night watch. The log says, in full: "Stars."
- Dev Raman flew the Tern round the bay for practice. Very gently. Nobody spilled anything.
- The bridge thanks Works for the new chair. The old one squeaked. The Commander noticed.
- Survey has named a new star after the ship's tea corner. Unofficially. Very unofficially.
? weekday:wed
- Midweek: the ship's on course, the coils are calm, and the Commander is on his day off.
? weekday:sun
- Sunday on the bridge: quiet, steady, one very long cup of tea.

== news.galley
- Brennan wants it known that gravy is not a drink. She has seen things.
- Today's soup: lentil. Brennan's note: "It's good for you. Eat it anyway."
- The galley is out of mustard. Brennan is in mourning. Normal service soon.
- Ivo Madsen has been banned from naming the specials. "Mystery Tuesday" was the last straw.
- The cooks thank everyone for coming to dinner on time. It helps more than you know.
- Fresh bread at breakfast. If you smell it on Deck 4, that's not a dream.
- The galley would like its big ladle back. It knows who has it. It's waiting.
- Esme Walsh caught a spelling mistake on the menu board. It said "chili con carnie". Fixed.
- Brennan tasted the porridge and said "fine". From Brennan, that's a medal.
- Please tell the galley if you can't eat something. They'll make you something you can.
? time:morning
- Breakfast is on till 08:00. Porridge, eggs, toast, tea. Brennan says don't skip it.
? time:evening
- Dinner's on till half eight. There's still pudding. There's always still pudding.

== news.works
- The parts racks have been counted. Two washers short. Works suspects the cart.
- The machine shop thanks whoever swept up. It was beautiful. They nearly cried.
- Coil one and coil two: humming. Coil three: thinking about it.
- Emeka Halloran told a joke at the tea corner. Works has asked for it not to happen again.
- Theo Teague fixed a fault in eight minutes. He wants a medal. He's getting a biscuit.
- Bea Silva found the squeak in the Cart bay. It was a wheel. It's always a wheel.
- The engine watch room has a new kettle. Engine crew are calling it a "major refit".
- Zainab Kovac has polished every panel on Deck 5. Every one. Please don't touch them.
- Femi Rossi and Farah Rahman raced to clear the board. Femi says he won. Farah disputes it.
- Works' monthly report: fewer faults, faster fixes, and more biscuits eaten than ever.
? weekday:wed
- Midweek check: the job board is half empty. Or half full. Ask the Chief which.

== news.garden
- The garden's sunflowers have turned to face the lights. They're very loyal.
- Gerald the cactus in the garden has flowered. Gerald has never been happier.
- The gardeners have built a new trellis. The beans are climbing it like they mean it.
- Mint is everywhere. The gardeners are sorry. They can't stop it. Nobody can.
- The compost is doing well, says Tove. Tove is very proud of the compost.
- Peppers! Small ones, red ones, hot ones. Ask before you bite. Ask Ravi.
? time:morning
- The garden lights are at dawn. It's the best time for a walk. Bring your tea.

== news.infirmary
- The infirmary's step counter challenge has begun. Rina is winning. Rina is always winning.
- Dr. Nandakumar has stopped the cold in its tracks. Mostly. Keep washing your hands.
- Reminder: if you feel off, come in. It's what the infirmary is for.
- Elif Yoon has the night shift in the infirmary. Bumps after ten go to Elif.
- Health checks are going well. Most of you drink enough water. Most.

== news.trad
? trad:running
- Running club: Vance did twelve laps and complained about the eleventh. Join them.
? trad:quiz
- Tonight's quiz has a round on the Wren. Know your decks. Know your cacti.
? trad:film
- Film night verdict: half cried, half slept, one person cheered at the wrong moment.
? trad:observatory-night
- Observatory night: a clear sky. Sato found a new comet and named it after the kettle.
? trad:market
- The swap meet's best trade this week: a scarf for a song. A whole song. Sung live.
? trad:hull-lights
- Hull-lights tonight. The bow lounge fills fast. Get there early or stand at the back.
? trad:jam
- The jam had three guitars, two spoons and one very brave singer. A great night.

== news.crew
? birthday:me
- {name} is a year older today. Wish them happy birthday at dinner. Cake's on.
? newhere
- Say hello to {first}. They're new, and the lift's still a mystery to them.
? dept:works
- {name} in Works kept the lights on all week. You didn't notice. That's the point.
? dept:helm
- {name} at the helm has kept us steady all week. Steady is good. Steady is lovely.
? dept:comms
- {name} in Comms got three calls home through the relay queue. Thank them later.

== news.gossip
- Overheard in the laundry: "Whose is this?" "Nobody's." "It's got a name tag."
- Overheard at breakfast: "Why is the toast cold?" "You took twenty minutes to choose."
- Overheard in the music room: "Know this song?" "Everyone knows this song." "I don't."
- Overheard in the corridor: "Is it Tuesday?" "It's Thursday." "Since when?"
- Overheard in the Works bay: "It's not broken. It's thinking." "Since when?" "Monday."
- Word on Deck 2: the telescope's lost lens cap has been found. In the telescope.
- Word on Deck 3: somebody asked Brennan for her secret recipe. They're still recovering.
- Word on Deck 6: the engine room is warmer than ever. The engine crew have stopped moaning.
- Rumour has it Survey keeps a secret biscuit tin. Rumour also has it the tin is empty.
- Rumour has it Gerald the cactus has a twin. Every Gerald denies it.

== news.outside
- Outside: a slow, sparkling stream of ice. Survey says it's a comet's tail. We say lovely.
- Outside: twin moons on a pale planet. Nobody lives there. It's still nice to wave.
- Outside: a bright stripe of stars across the stern. Best seen from the junior common room.
- Outside: a dark nebula hiding the stars. Inside it, says Survey, stars are being born.
- Outside: a yellow star, a lot like home for some of us. Look for a while.
- Outside: a field of asteroids, far off and harmless. Helm is keeping a polite distance.

== news.notice
- Found: one glove, Deck 3 gym. Lonely. Cold. Ask at the crew store.
- Found: a library book from the junior common room, in the garden. It had a nice time.
- Lost: a cactus. Not Gerald. A different cactus. Also called Gerald.
- Wanted: a tea partner for long afternoons. Must like biscuits. Apply at the tea corner.
- Wanted: anyone who knows the words to the third verse. The jam needs you.
- Offered: one slightly used rowing machine. Kidding, it's the gym's. It's free to use.
- Notice: please don't feed the garden's fish. There are no fish. Please stop looking.
- Notice: lost property is at the crew store. Most of it is socks.
- Thank you to whoever pinned "well done, everyone" on the job board. We needed it.
- Reminder: the bow lounge windows are for looking, not leaning. Works will tell you why.
